 neighbor's dog for a walk  because they're too scared to go out and  do it themselves is that okay  it should be the case that that that  neighbor should do the dog walking  themselves we should minimize contact  between a  solds if you've got dogs at home and you  want to walk that dog of course you  should walk that dog but only one walk  or one other exercise a day I'm taking a  total for a walk in the park and there  are already other parents gathering in  large numbers do I contact the  authorities  you should wherever possible try to  encourage people not to gather in that  way and if you are genuinely worried  then of course contact the authorities  but it should be the case that if you  are for example going for a walk in the  park with a member of your immediate  family and you see other people  gathering in that way then if you can  you should try to seek to get them to  recognize the clear guidance that the  government is given you misspoke earlier  about what should happen to children who  have separated can you just clarify the  situation yes absolutely I was asked on  another program on piers morgan's good  morning Britain program about this and I  was not clear and thank you for giving  me the opportunity to be clear it is the  case that if you're divorced or  separated that and you and you have  children who are under the age of 18  those children can move from one parents  home to another parents home as  appropriate now we want to try to reduce  the amount of movement between homes but  that is a clear exception here and I I  want to make it clear that I was not  when I was being interviewed on Piers  Morgan's programme as clear as I should  have been in specifying that there is  this exception and also to be clear it's  Susanna Reed's program as well talk to  me about why these prime minister  decided to take the action that he did  last night why is it taking so long  though the promise of fall is scientific  advice and we act at the right time 